    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi @emcastillo! I've switched to Ubuntu 22.04 LTS and I believe I've pinpointed the issue I'm encountering. On Windows 10, when processing an array that doubled in size from 2^27 to 2^28 elements, the runtime became extremely slow. However, on Ubuntu, the same increase in array size results in an out-of-memory error. Here's the traceback:\r\n\r\n<pre>(py311) <font color=\"#26A269\"><b>eric@perseus</b></font>:<font color=\"#12488B\"><b>/media/eric/M33/py311</b></font>$ python3 ../core.py\r\n\r\n [2023-11-13 at 00:05:45] Job started\r\n\r\n [2023-11-13 at 00:06:13] Loop has started ... \r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File &quot;/media/eric/M33/py311/../core.py&quot;, line 90, in &lt;module&gt;\r\n    result = core()\r\n             ^^^^^^\r\n  File &quot;/media/eric/M33/py311/../core.py&quot;, line 61, in core\r\n    exp_Dop_h= cp.exp(Dop_s * h / 2.0)\r\n                      ~~~~~~~~~~^~~~~\r\n  File &quot;cupy/_core/core.pyx&quot;, line 1307, in cupy._core.core._ndarray_base.__truediv__\r\n  File &quot;cupy/_core/core.pyx&quot;, line 1676, in cupy._core.core._ndarray_base.__array_ufunc__\r\n  File &quot;cupy/_core/_kernel.pyx&quot;, line 1291, in cupy._core._kernel.ufunc.__call__\r\n  File &quot;cupy/_core/_kernel.pyx&quot;, line 644, in cupy._core._kernel._get_out_args_from_optionals\r\n  File &quot;cupy/_core/core.pyx&quot;, line 2765, in cupy._core.core._ndarray_init\r\n  File &quot;cupy/_core/core.pyx&quot;, line 241, in cupy._core.core._ndarray_base._init_fast\r\n  File &quot;cupy/cuda/memory.pyx&quot;, line 742, in cupy.cuda.memory.alloc\r\n  File &quot;cupy/cuda/memory.pyx&quot;, line 1419, in cupy.cuda.memory.MemoryPool.malloc\r\n  File &quot;cupy/cuda/memory.pyx&quot;, line 1440, in cupy.cuda.memory.MemoryPool.malloc\r\n  File &quot;cupy/cuda/memory.pyx&quot;, line 1120, in cupy.cuda.memory.SingleDeviceMemoryPool.malloc\r\n  File &quot;cupy/cuda/memory.pyx&quot;, line 1141, in cupy.cuda.memory.SingleDeviceMemoryPool._malloc\r\n  File &quot;cupy/cuda/memory.pyx&quot;, line 1379, in cupy.cuda.memory.SingleDeviceMemoryPool._try_malloc\r\ncupy.cuda.memory.OutOfMemoryError: Out of memory allocating 4,294,967,296 bytes (allocated so far: 21,474,838,528 bytes).\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\nMonitoring GPU memory allocation with nvidia-smi, I observed that my RTX 4090 really runs out of memory when handling the 2^28 element array, while it manages the 2^27 element array with a memory usage of 19233MiB out of 24564MiB. This suggests that Windows manages GPU memory differently, likely by utilizing swap space, which allows the process to continue but at a significantly reduced speed\r\n\r\nI will mount a new setup with two GPUs soon, and I will let you know about the outcome. Regarding using two GPUs, could you please let me know if you have any recommendations beyond what is in the documentation?\r\n\r\nThank you very much for your help!\r\n",
