    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Sorry I missed the ping. I cannot find a public reference for this behavior, but it is known that on Windows instead of hitting OOM, the OS would try to spill into system memory, and the slowness (of any kernel, not just cuFFT) is a consequence. Generally, when using large arrays one should be cautious about potential memory and overflow issues, and reports like this would help us triage/understand better, so thanks! \ud83d\ude42  ",
