  {
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Thanks for confirming. Yes, `cupy.cuda.MemoryPool.set_limit()` is equivalent to `CUPY_GPU_MEMORY_LIMIT`, so pick whatever is most convenient to you.\r\n\r\nFor multi GPUs, in the future the new distributed ndarray would be useful, but it doesn't support FFT yet. For now you need to partition the work and manage the per-GPU data chunks manually.\r\n\r\nClosing, since the original issue is resolved.",
